# Database & backups
/db/
/db/backups/
# Out-of-band pre-migration snapshots live in a SIBLING of this repo
# (../db-snapshots/), which is where every one of them has been taken. This
# anchored pattern exists because the obvious mistake is to create the folder
# HERE, one `git add .` away from committing a copy of the production
# database. Anchored, per C-26b (Batch 0.1): a bare pattern would swallow any
# directory of that name at any depth.
/db-snapshots/

# `/upload/` was an empty stray directory, ignored for tidiness. It was deleted
# on 2026-09-11 — KEEP THIS ENTRY ANYWAY: it is what stops the stray from being
# re-created and committed.
#
# It is NOT where the images live, and this comment used to claim that user
# uploads "must not be committed" — which reads as a policy about
# `public/uploads/`, where the catalogue's real images sit and ARE tracked:
# 147 files, 49 293 837 bytes, measured 2026-09-11. DD-16 (2026-09-05) decided
# to keep them tracked. The reason given here used to be "and no restorable
# backup exists (L-46)" — L-46 CLOSED on 2026-09-11: two encrypted backups in
# `db/backups/` have been verified by decryption and their media archive IS
# `public/uploads/`. They are on the same disk as the database they protect,
# which is why git still earns its place as the off-tree copy.
# Do not add public/uploads/ here.
/upload/

# Z.ai artifacts
_archive/
download/
agent-ctx/
worklog.md

# Playwright output (Batch 6.3). `test-results/` is the default outputDir and
# holds traces and screenshots of failures; CI uploads it as an artifact
# (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`). It is regenerated every run. Anchored, per C-26b.
#
# `/playwright-report/` is kept as a guard, not as a description: nothing
# produces it today, because `playwright.config.ts` sets `reporter: "list"`,
# which writes no HTML report. Switching to the `html` reporter would create it
# — that is what this line is here for. (The comment above used to say "Both are
# regenerated every run", which was true of only one of them.)
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
